==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor [[Toon]] bring {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}} to the elevator to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Gigi is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the third requirement, focus on going on multiple runs, and try to get the {{CDI|Avaricious/Covetous|name=true}} cards, since they increase the chance of rare [[Items]] appearing in [[Dandy's Shop]] or on the ground of the [[Floors]]. The further you advance, the chance becomes higher.

==[[Toon of the Week]] Quests==
{{TOTWQuests|Retrieve 10 items from {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}}'s stash.|Acquire 30 items from Gigi's [[Ability]].|Find Gigi's arcade game on [[Vee's Floor]].}}

===Rewards===
*1 Quest completed: {{AT|Gigi Fan}} [[Title]]
*2 Quests completed: {{SI|Golden Gigi!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]
*3 Quests completed: {{Skin|Golden Gacha|toon=Gigi}} [[Skin]]

===Strategies===
*For the first Quest, play the game normally with distractor like {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Looey|name=true}}, or {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} or fast extractors like {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, or {{CI|Vee|name=true}} to progress through the [[Floors]] faster. Some recommended trinkets are speed [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}} or {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}, cooldown-reduction Trinkets like {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} or {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}, and extracting Trinkets like {{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}, {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}, or {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}. Do those until you've found {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}} on the same floor, when you do, you will find her stash to retrieve your items, there it looks like a claw machine with gachapons inside them, once you've found the stash, grab the items that are released out the machine and grab them until you have 10. Solo runs is best for this since you can grab the items easily without other players having to grab them. But, if you have a team, it is recommended to form a line and take turns grabbing items until they have 10. 

*For the second Quest, play as Gigi, and use Sweet Charm and/or Ghost Snakes In A Can as well as picking the {{CDI|Rehearsal/Practice|name=true}} Cards to reduce the 60 second cooldown (you can also use {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}'s {{AI|Waxwell|name=true}} [[Ability]] to help you with cooldown). Alternatively, you can find an afk spot on any map and stay there and spam the {{AI|Gigi|name=true}} Ability 30 times (or use an autoclicker).

*For the third Quest, progress through Floors with the same strategies as the first quest, but now try to encounter [[Vee's Floor]]. Once you've encountered her Floor, try to find the out of order gachapon claw machine (similar to Twisted Gigi's stash except it has no [[Ichor]]) around the arcade rooms. When you found it, get in front of the out of order machine with caution tape (Playing as Gigi will have dialogue pop up above her head).

==Strategies==
Gigi is excellent at extracting [[Machines]] with her 5{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(250 Skill Check Size, 3.00 Skill Check Value, 25% Skill Check Chance and 5 Skill Check Speed)}}, and has average [[Movement Speed]], [[Stealth]], and [[Extraction Speed]]. Her only disadvantage is her 1 Star [[Stamina]], which makes it difficult to escape from [[Twisteds]]. It is highly recommended to use both {{CDI|Well-Paced/Endurance|name=true}} [[Cards]] to increase her Stamina to 120. Prioritizing Stamina [[Items]] (such as {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false|plural=a}}/{{II|Protein Bar|name=false|plural=a}}) over speed ones may be beneficial as well.

Her Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Gigi}}'''Surprise!''', depends on luck. She can get rare items such as {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s, {{II|Eject Button|name=false}}s, and {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false}}s from this Ability. Storing these rare items can be useful, keeping a Smoke Bomb for fast Twisteds, or a {{II|Bottle o' Pop|name=false}} if she exhausts while being chased. Her Ability is weighted towards rarer Items somewhat so you won't have to use it too often in order to get such Items. You can additionally use {{TI|Lucky Coin|name=true}} if you want to get rarer Items more consistently, by removing Common Items from the pool. Notably, {{TI|Bone|name=true}}, {{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}}, and {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}} will activate every time she uses her Ability, and can be equipped to make it a more reliable buff.

Note that you only get an Item after the spin wheel lands on a specific Item's section, but the Ability is counted as activated (when you get +5 [[Ichor]] and activate certain Trinkets) when you press the Ability button.

Remember, though useful, '''Surprise!''' has the potential to be a disadvantage as well, capable of clogging up Gigi's inventory with items that are not immediately discardable.{{II|Stopwatch|name=false}}es, {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}}s, {{II|Instructions|name=false}}, and {{II|Valve|name=false}}s should be used as soon as possible; if Gigi is not distracting, the same should be done with {{II|Air Horn|name=false}}s, though with caution. With healing items, counter-intuitively, it's better to store more mobility items, as her low Stamina makes her at danger of taking more damage without them and requiring more healing than she would've otherwise.  At least one slot should be reserved for mobility or immediately usable items at all times. Weigh carefully whether having a slot locked up is a threat before using her Ability. Items that are more common, such as {{II|Gumballs|name=false}}, {{II|Chocolate|name=false}}s, {{II|Stealth Candy|name=false|plural=a}}, and {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}} can help her farm [[Tapes]] and leave more space in her inventory.

Gigi solos are a great option with her 5 Star Skill Check. She can buff that stat even more by equipping {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}, which maximizes it at 4.80/4.60 Skill Check value. The disadvantage to soloing Gigi is her Stamina, which makes it hard to get out of a Twisted's line of sight, quickly depleting her Stamina and getting her hit. This can be mitigated by using {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}, to buff her Run Speed. {{TI|Speedometer|name=true}} can also help, as it gives her +15 Stamina, which in addition to both Well-Paced/Endurance Cards can boost her Stamina by 1 Star. Alternatively, {{TI|Cooler|name=true}}  can be helpful, giving her 2 Star Stamina at the cost of -5% speed, which can be mitigated by mobility Items or a Speed Trinket. Completing {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}'s Floor when the card crops up can boost her Stamina even further, though it can be time-consuming and risky to more inexperienced players.

Do note that the pre-run shop can already provide Bandages, {{II|Health Kit|name=false}}s, and Valves, which slightly devalues Gigi's Ability to players who have the Ichor. However, those Items are a one-time use, while her Ability could spawn them multiple times. Stay wary of the randomness of her Ability, as it is likely she could receive an unhelpful item rather than a helpful one.

