==Trivia==
*Gigi is the third non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] to have 5{{Star}} on a [[Stat]].
*Prior to [[Changelog|v0.4.1]], Gigi had 1 Star [[Movement Speed]] and 3 Star [[Stamina]], but it got swapped to 3 Star Movement Speed and 1 Star Stamina due to complaints about her gameplay.
**Gigi is the only non-[[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to receive a [[Stat]] rework.
**Coincidentally, {{CI|Connie|name=true}}, the next Toon to release, has that exact Star Spread in her Movement Speed and Stamina.
*Gigi, along with {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, {{CI|Finn|name=true}}, and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, are one of the only [[Toons]] to not have a full icon.
*Gigi is the first [[Toon]] to be teased outside of the game, unless you count {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} himself, who was shown on an arcade machine in [[W:C:flavorfrenzy|Flavor Frenzy]] (BlushCrunch Studio's other game) before [[Dandy's World]]'s release.
*Gigi is the only [[Toon]] to not have visible hands.
**However, it is possible to see arm marks under her sweater, so maybe she just keeps her hands inside her sweater all the time.
*Gigi is the first [[Toon]] to be released on their own, with the second being [[Yatta]], the third being [[Blot]], the fourth being {{CI|Squirm|name=true}}, and the fifth being {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}.
**However, according to Qwel back in February 2025, due to the [[Main Character]] Toons optimizations not being finished quickly enough to all release together, she said they'd add a Toon earlier than originally planned.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/970049062608961560/1344802320482959371</ref> Since [[Yatta]] was the next Toon added since that statement, it is likely that she and Blot were originally intended to release together, making Gigi the first [[Toon]] to be released on their own and be planned as such.
*Gigi is the second [[Toon]] to have sleeves.
**Gigi has the longest sleeves out of everyone, with the reason being that [[Qwel]] was reminded of the fact that {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} was originally the only Toon with sleeves, leading her to design Gigi with "BIG" sleeves.<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1369623850035318887</ref>
*Gigi is the second [[Toon]] whose head can open up, with the first being {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}.
**Their [[Twisted]] counterparts both have [[Ichor]] hands going through those parts.
*Gigi seems to be a hoarder and/or a collector, as shown in her dialogues in the [[Elevator]] and in her interactions with {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}, and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}.
**Adding on, her interaction with Vee may imply that Gigi could be somewhat of a thief as well and hoards random things that she finds. Her interactions with [[Connie]] and {{CI|Astro|name=true}} could also contribute to this.
**It also seems she hides her stuff in random spots of [[Gardenview]] with one of her interactions with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}.
*Gigi is good friends with {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, owing to the fact she gifted the {{TI|Diary|name=true}} to her, holds onto it for safe keeping, and that she is allowed to write in her Diary for her. She also gets along well with [[Connie]], [[Poppy]] and overall most of the girls.
*Gigi is the second [[Toon]] to have a transparent part on their head, with the first being [[Rodger]].
**This allows them to be used to see [[Blackouts]] clearer, but because Gigi's head is made of a different, more translucent material, it's less effective.
*Similar to {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, Gigi doesn't wear shoes, and the lighter color on the soles of her feet are actually markings.<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1420792830963744798 https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1420793532007841956</ref>
*Gigi is the third [[Toon]] whose [[Ability]] name ends in an exclamation mark, with the first being {{CI|Goob|name=true}} and {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, the second being [[Tisha]], and the fourth being {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}.
*Gigi is the first [[Toon]] to produce [[Items]] in any way, with the second being [[Yatta]], and the third being {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}.
**She is the only one whose [[Ability]] doesn't drop Items.
*Gigi was the first non-[[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to appear on the game icon, as well as the first and currently only of which to appear more than once the game icon.
**She is also the second Toon to appear on the game icon with a [[Skin]].
**She is the only playable Toon in the game to appear on the game icon three times.
*Gigi is the last [[Toon]] to release with an unoptimized model.
*Gigi can carry [[Toodles]] in her head, as shown in a storyboard.<ref>[[File:Connie, Gigi, and Toodles Storyboard.png|200px]]</ref>
**This implies that she can carry other [[Toons]] smaller or with a similar size as Toodles, like [[Pebble]] and {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}.
*Contrary to popular belief, Gigi's [[Ability]] can't give all [[Items]] in the game, with {{II|BonBons|name=false}}, {{II|Dandy Easter Egg|name=false}}s, {{II|Christmas Cookie|name=false}}s, and {{II|Dandy Corn|name=false}} being unobtainable. This misconception is likely caused by the fact the [[Cards]] {{CDI|Blind Grab/Lost and Found|name=false}} are able to grant you this Item and her Ability description bring slightly misleading about giving any Item.
*Gigi and [[Brusha]] are the only [[Toons]] to have their eyes naturally half-lidded due to their head shapes.
*Gigi and [[Toodles]] may be friends, as seen in their interactions with each other and their appearance in a storyboard together.
**This is further strengthened by how they live on the same floor and their [[Ability]] similarities, which are both luck-related and use to share the same sound effect.
***This sound originates from the [[w:C:roblox:Catalog:Banana Peel|Banana Peel Gear]].
***During [[Changelog|v0.28.1]] Gigi's ability sound was changed to match with her new wheel spin VFX.
*Prior to [[Changelog|v0.13.14]], Gigi was one of the three unoptimized [[Toons]] to not be released during the launch while also having no appearances in any posters during the launch prior to release, with the others being [[Finn]] and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}.
*Gigi, along with [[Rodger]], are the fourth [[Toons]] to appear on 2 separate thumbnails, being [[Changelog|v0.4]] and v0.13.14, with the first being [[Pebble]], the second being {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, the third being [[Toodles]], the fifth being [[Bobette]], and the sixth being the rest of the [[Christmas Toons]]. 
*In Gigi's interaction with [[Finn]], he mentions the star-fish, likely reflecting how she has a star on her sweater.
**In the same interaction, she pretends to show interest in what he says. This is likely a reference to how [[Connie]] does the same thing in her interaction with Finn, however, Connie tricks him, saying it was still boring.
*Prior to Gigi's interaction with [[Teagan]], when she mentions about one of her bags of sugar being missing, Gigi might actually be telling the truth this time, as [[Yatta]] loves sweets, therefore, she might have took the bag of sugar.
*If you enter the [[Gift Shop]] as Gigi and go to the Trading Cards area, she will say "{{Text|Oh yeaaah, I have all the super ultra rare cards in my room! I'm pretty much the best collector.}}".<ref>[[File:Gigi Gift Shop Dialogue.png|200px]]</ref>
*Gigi uses the same prank on {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and [[Sprout]] on their dialogues together, that being the "It says gullible on the ceiling" prank, though unlike Sprout, Cosmo falls for it.
*Gigi is the third [[Toon]] who uses their head to store or contain something, being items she's stolen, the first being [[Teagan]], the second being [[Finn]], and the fourth being {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}.
*Gigi is the fifth [[Toon]] to get a [[Toon of the Week]], as well as the third female, and first {{Type|Rare}} to get one.
**She is also the first Toon to have their Deluxe Plush released on the same day as their first Toon of the Week.
**She is also the first Toon to have their lore video to not be on a TV and instead it is on what looks to be a modified Sneaky Gigi arcade machine.
**She is the first Toon to appear in the Game Icon with a [[Skin]] for their Toon of the Week.
*Gigi's new render, added in [[Changelog|v0.28.3]], was leaked in an earlier update, being v0.27.1, as [[Profiles]] can show a [[Toons]]' full render, but instead of using the render had at the time her new render was used by accident.
**This render was still lacking in other places like in the game itself, not resolving itself until a later date.
*Gigi's head could hold an infinite amount of [[Items]] due to her head being a {{wp|Hammerspace}} according to one of her and [[Rodger]]'s interactions.
*In [[Vee's Floor]], Gigi has 2 arcade games, being Sneaky Gigi and a Gigi-themed gachapon claw machine which are all out of order.
**Before [[Changelog|v0.28.1]], 3 of the Sneaky Gigi arcade machines took its place.
**A variant of the claw machines can be seen on any [[Floor]] as long as [[Twisted Gigi]] is on the Floor, with this version being as her stash. This version of the machine is covered in [[Ichor]] and has a hole in the top and, unlike the out of order ones, these ones are functional.
***The music that plays is an 8-Bit version of Clair de Lune.
*Gigi appears in the second most thumbnails compared to other [[Toons]], only losing to [[Dandy]].
**She appears in the thumbnails for [[Changelog|v0.4]], v0.13.14, v0.21, and v0.28.

